  "Coordinates: 'published coordinate' values come from Wikipedia/Wikidata; others are estimated by fitting the German Wikipedia location sketch (Vorlage:Tal der Könige (Ost)) to 27 published coordinates (median error about 15 m). Treat all positions as approximate entrances, good for a map at 30 m terrain resolution, not for survey use.",
  "begun_bce is the start of the owner's reign (I. Shaw, Oxford History of Ancient Egypt), used to order the timeline; it is not an exact construction date. null means unknown.",
  "KV65 (a radar anomaly reported in 2008) and KVF are not included: they are not confirmed tombs.",
  "Facts summarise Wikipedia's tomb list and individual tomb articles (English and German); tomb plans and maps of the Theban Mapping Project are NOT copied.",
  "discovered_year: first year the tomb was recorded by modern visitors (for 'before 1739' etc. the year given). discovered_era is 'antiquity' for tombs open since ancient times (Greek and Roman graffiti prove visits), 'modern', or 'unknown'. Event 'year' values below 0 are BCE."
